<title>ITALY: Italy's Turin sees Sept CPI at 2.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Turin sees Sept CPI at 2.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Turin said its September consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.9 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Turin's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 3.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Turin is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 8.81 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.1)     2.9  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.2  (-0.2)     4.3  (4.8)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1   (0.0)     5.1  (5.0)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.6   (0.5)     3.3  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0  (-0.1)     1.0  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Health services		  -0.2   (0.0)     0.8  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0   (0.2)     3.0  (3.2)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.0   (0.2)     3.6  (3.6)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.9   (0.0)     5.1  (4.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.1)     1.4  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1   (0.3)     2.4  (2.3)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
